core_margin_advantage":0.0,"_gate_pool_share":null,"_gp_pool_share":null,"_score_pool_share":null,"_gate_rev_durability":0.04138548844310663,"_gp_rev_durability":true,"_score_rev_durability":45.7,"_gate_fcf_durability":0.44372757357592163,"_gp_fcf_durability":true,"_score_fcf_durability":100.0,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":0.0,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":null,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":null,"_score_shrhldr_yield":0.0,"_gate_share_shrink":0.16844448154633307,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.057071813973601705,"_gp_sbc_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":4.9,"_gate_insider_own":0.109110005,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":72.7,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"Ready Capital Corporation operates as a real estate finance company in the United States. The company operates through two segments: LMM Commercial Real Estate and Small Business Lending. Its LMM Commercial Real Estate segment originates LLM loans across the full life-cycle of an LLM property, including construction, bridge, stabilized, and agency loan origination channels. The Small Business Lending segment acquires, originates, and services owner-occupied loans guaranteed by the SBA under its SBA Section 7(a) Program; and originates, and services USDA loans, as well as small business loans. The company originates, acquires, finances, and services lower-to-middle-market (LLM) commercial real estate loans, small business administration (SBA) loans, residential mortgage loans, construction loans, USDA loans, and mortgage-backed securities collateralized primarily by LLM loans, or other real estate-related investments. It has elected to be taxed as a real estate investment trust (REIT) and would not be subject to federal corporate income taxes if it distributes at least 90% of its taxable income to its stockholders. The company was formerly known as Sutherland Asset Management Corporation and changed its name to Ready Capital Corporation in September 2018. Ready Capital Corporation was founded in 2007 and is headquartered in New York, New York.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Thomas Edward Capasse | Chairman, CEO & Chief Investment Officer | Age 68","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 400 people. Revenue per employee of $254K ranks in the bottom quartile among Real Estate peers, with revenue growing 16%/yr across its filed history. Stock-based compensation of $15K per employee reflects an ownership culture. Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (9/10).","financial_summary":["Ready Capital Corporation is a micro-cap real estate business with a $132M market cap on $102M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -42% over the past three years and +4% annually across the full decade, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at 9% against a 10% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","On the balance sheet, thin -0.6\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Insiders hold 11% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (-0.2) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Revenue growth in the bottom decile of Real Estate peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"red","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Operating margins 320% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Elevated short interest (12.9% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 73/100): leveraged balance sheet under pressure; roic below cost of capital \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"Interest-rate sensitivity and tenant-credit risk \u2014 cap rates and refinancing costs move faster than the 10-year leases can absorb.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Climate and insurance cost escalation \u2014 rising premiums and coverage withdrawals in flood/fire zones are repricing assets that the market once treated as perpetuities.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Reviewing Ready Capital (RC) & The Competition","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/13/reviewing-ready-capital-rc-the-competition.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794569137.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.922,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Ready Capital (NYSE:RC) Stock Gets Price Target Trim from UBS Group","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/12/ready-capital-nyserc-stock-gets-price-target-trim-from-ubs-group.html","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794498899.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.807,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["analyst_action"]},{"title":"Richmond Machinist's Giant RC Buggy Wins Grand Prize in Metal Supermarkets' Annual Metal My Way Contest","source":"